.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/numerical_analysis/approximation/plot_03_remez_minimax`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Chebyshev&#x27;s least-deviation polynomials suggest placing interpolation nodes at the extrema of T_n(x) = \cos(n \arccos x), which cluster toward the ends of [-1, 1]. At these nodes the Lebesgue constant grows only logarithmically, so the interpolant of Runge&#x27;s function 1/(1+25x^2) converges as the degree rises. This script shows the node clustering, the degree-20 Chebyshev interpolant, and its error shrinking geometrically.">

.. only:: html

